1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,070
Chai Corner now has five
outlets and a small head office.

2
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:07,109
But every small decision
still waits for Ravi.

3
00:00:07,659 --> 00:00:10,476
At outlet two, a customer wants a refund.

4
00:00:10,476 --> 00:00:12,139
Meena has to call Ravi.

5
00:00:12,439 --> 00:00:13,909
The milk runs low.

6
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:15,643
Meena calls Ravi again.

7
00:00:15,943 --> 00:00:19,972
Ravi gets forty calls a day, and
customers wait while he answers.

8
00:00:20,622 --> 00:00:22,253
Ravi cannot do it all.

9
00:00:22,253 --> 00:00:23,776
He needs to delegate.

10
00:00:24,476 --> 00:00:26,953
So, what is delegation of authority?

11
00:00:27,253 --> 00:00:31,855
Delegation means a manager gives a
team member the authority to do a task,

12
00:00:31,855 --> 00:00:33,974
and to make decisions about it.

13
00:00:34,574 --> 00:00:39,124
So Ravi tells Meena: from today, you
approve refunds and order supplies

14
00:00:39,124 --> 00:00:40,261
at outlet two.

15
00:00:40,911 --> 00:00:43,239
Delegation has three linked parts.

16
00:00:43,689 --> 00:00:44,589
One.

17
00:00:44,232 --> 00:00:45,358
Responsibility.

18
00:00:45,358 --> 00:00:47,877
This is the duty given to someone.

19
00:00:47,877 --> 00:00:50,715
Meena must keep outlet two running well.

20
00:00:51,065 --> 00:00:51,965
Two.

21
00:00:51,595 --> 00:00:52,495
Authority.

22
00:00:52,435 --> 00:00:55,061
This is the power to act and decide.

23
00:00:55,061 --> 00:00:59,535
Meena can approve a refund, or
order milk, without calling Ravi.

24
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:00,785
Three.

25
00:01:00,512 --> 00:01:01,602
Accountability.

26
00:01:01,602 --> 00:01:04,553
This means being
answerable for the results.

27
00:01:04,553 --> 00:01:07,133
Every Friday, Meena reports to Ravi.

28
00:01:07,783 --> 00:01:08,973
Now the key rule.

29
00:01:08,973 --> 00:01:11,209
What moves down, and what stays up?

30
00:01:11,559 --> 00:01:13,531
Authority can be delegated.

31
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,739
Ravi passes it down to Meena.

32
00:01:16,089 --> 00:01:19,165
Responsibility is assigned,
and Meena accepts it.

33
00:01:19,515 --> 00:01:21,928
But accountability cannot be delegated.

34
00:01:22,278 --> 00:01:25,741
If outlet two has a bad
month, Meena answers to Ravi.

35
00:01:25,741 --> 00:01:28,664
But Ravi still answers
for all of Chai Corner.

36
00:01:29,314 --> 00:01:31,759
One more rule: the principle of parity.

37
00:01:32,109 --> 00:01:34,572
Authority must match responsibility.

38
00:01:34,922 --> 00:01:39,181
If Meena must keep the milk stocked,
but cannot spend a single rupee, she

39
00:01:39,181 --> 00:01:40,340
is sure to fail.

40
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:44,250
So Ravi lets her spend up to
five thousand rupees a day.

41
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:46,828
Enough power for the job, and no more.

42
00:01:47,478 --> 00:01:48,831
So why delegate?

43
00:01:49,181 --> 00:01:50,775
It frees the manager.

44
00:01:50,775 --> 00:01:53,868
Ravi now gets five calls a day, not forty.

45
00:01:54,218 --> 00:01:55,791
It develops the team.

46
00:01:55,791 --> 00:01:58,253
Meena learns to make real decisions.

47
00:01:58,603 --> 00:02:00,258
And decisions get faster.

48
00:02:00,258 --> 00:02:03,044
A refund now takes one minute, not twenty.

49
00:02:03,694 --> 00:02:04,664
Quick check.

50
00:02:04,664 --> 00:02:07,595
Meena approves a wrong
refund at outlet two.

51
00:02:07,595 --> 00:02:09,585
Who is ultimately accountable?

52
00:02:11,485 --> 00:02:12,385
Ravi!

53
00:02:12,096 --> 00:02:16,779
Accountability cannot be delegated,
so the manager stays answerable.

54
00:02:17,379 --> 00:02:18,388
So, remember.

55
00:02:18,688 --> 00:02:22,977
Delegation means giving a team
member the authority to do a task.

56
00:02:23,327 --> 00:02:27,937
It links responsibility, authority,
and accountability, and authority must

57
00:02:27,937 --> 00:02:29,363
match responsibility.

58
00:02:29,713 --> 00:02:33,798
Authority moves down, but
accountability stays with the manager.

59
00:02:34,398 --> 00:02:38,946
Next time, we'll ask how much power
should stay at the head office, with

60
00:02:38,946 --> 00:02:41,132
centralization and decentralization.
